## TOOL-33 — 2026-04-19

State: mid-merge
Failure: git pull --no-rebase origin main during /ship conflicted because local main had the new TOOL-33 charter (run-quality fixes + TOOL-34) while origin/main still had the old charter (GitHub Issues POC). The two charters diverged before the feature branch was created, so the pull created a two-sided conflict in docs/roadmap-core.md and docs/task-index.md.
Resolution: Kept HEAD (local main) for all conflicts — it had the correct, up-to-date charter. Committed the resolved merge, then merged the feature branch cleanly, updated docs to mark TOOL-33 done, archived the plan.
Pattern: charter-divergence — local main has a newer charter than origin/main when the feature branch was already created from local main. Safe resolution: always prefer HEAD (local main) in docs/ conflicts when origin/main's version predates the feature branch's base commit.

